  "abstract_cn": "以生成式人工智能（AIGC）为引擎的视听媒资管理正重塑广电传媒领域，论文聚焦“H平台”实践，系统梳理AIGC在内容创作、虚拟播报、融媒分发、数字资产估值的技术路径与商业闭环。通过参考文献、多个案例研究发现现实问题，通过PEST分析、波特五力分析等方法，提出对应解决方法。\n随着生成式人工智能（AIGC）技术的爆发式跃迁，广电行业正经历从“人工主导”向“人机协同”的范式重构。然而，技术在重塑内容生产流程、提升效率的同时，也引发了版权归属模糊、内容质量不可控、伦理边界冲突及商业模式不清晰等多重困境。本文以L公司推出的传媒垂类大模型平台“H”为典型案例，运用PEST及波特五力等工商管理学分析工具，深入剖析AIGC在广电领域的应用现状与核心痛点。\n研究发现，当前广电行业在数字化转型中面临技术成熟度不足与组织变革滞后的结构性矛盾，特别是在内容创作的版权风险、虚拟播报的受众信任危机、融媒分发的算法偏见以及数字资产估值的标准化缺失等方面存在显著挑战。针对上述问题，“H”平台提出了系统性的应对策略：在技术层面，构建“有中生有”、“智能标注”与“场景理解”三大核心能力，通过垂类大模型深耕与5G+超高清技术融合，解决通用模型在专业场景下的适配难题；在商业模式上，创新“共创平台”机制，打通“创作—展示—交易—落地”的全链条闭环，聚焦广电全生态、智能短剧与创新文旅三大赋能领域，实现从成本中心向价值中心的转变；在风险管控方面，确立“合规先行”原则，建立内容安全智能审核与数据隐私双重保护机制，确保技术应用符合意识形态安全要求。\n本文结论表明，“H”模式的成功关键在于实现了从单一技术应用到生态化运营的范式跃迁。其通过垂直深耕行业Know-how、场景驱动反向定义技术能力以及构建多方共赢的生态体系，为广电机构破解AIGC应用困境提供了可复制的路径参考。研究进一步指出，主流媒体的系统性变革需构建“技术-制度-人才”协同体系，在守正创新中动态平衡意识形态安全与技术演进，最终推动广电行业在新质生产力驱动下实现高质量可持续发展。",
  "abstract_en": "The management of audio-visual media assets driven by generative artificial intelligence (AIGC) is reshaping the field of radio and television media. This paper focuses on the practice of the \"H platform\" and systematically sorts out the technical paths and business closed loops of AIGC in content creation, virtual broadcasting, integrated media distribution, and digital asset valuation. Through references and multiple case studies, practical problems were identified. By means of PEST analysis, Porter's Five Forces analysis and other methods, corresponding solutions were proposed.\nWith the explosive leap of generative artificial intelligence (AIGC) technology, the broadcasting and television industry is undergoing a paradigm reconstruction from \"human-led\" to \"human-machine collaboration\". However, while technology is reshaping the content production process and enhancing efficiency, it has also brought about multiple predicaments such as ambiguous copyright ownership, uncontrollable content quality, ethical boundary conflicts, and unclear business models. This article takes the media vertical large model platform \"H\" launched by L Company as a typical case, and uses business administration analysis tools such as PEST and Porter's Five Forces to deeply analyze the current application status and core pain points of AIGC in the broadcasting and television field.\nResearch findings reveal that the current broadcasting and television industry is confronted with structural contradictions of insufficient technological maturity and lagging organizational change in its digital transformation. Particularly, there are significant challenges in areas such as copyright risks in content creation, audience trust crises in virtual broadcasting, algorithmic biases in integrated media distribution, and the lack of standardization in digital asset valuation. In response to the above issues, the \"H\" platform has proposed a systematic countermeasures: at the technical level, it builds three core capabilities: \"existing within existing\", \"intelligent annotation\", and \"scene understanding\". By deeply exploring vertical large models and integrating them with 5G+ ultra-high-definition technologies, it addresses the adaptation challenges of general models in professional scenarios. In terms of business model, innovate the \"co-creation platform\" mechanism, connect the full chain closed loop of \"creation - display - transaction - implementation\", focus on the three empowerment fields of the entire broadcasting and television ecosystem, intelligent short dramas and innovative cultural tourism, and achieve the transformation from a cost center to a value center. In terms of risk control, the principle of \"compliance first\" has been established, and a dual protection mechanism of intelligent content security review and data privacy has been set up to ensure that the application of technology complies with ideological security requirements.\nThe conclusion of this article indicates that the key to the success of the \"H\" model lies in achieving a paradigm leap from the application of a single technology to ecological operation. By vertically delving into industry Know-how, context-driven reverse definition of technical capabilities, and building a win-win ecosystem for all parties, it provides a replicable path reference for broadcasting and television institutions to break through the application predicament of AIGC. The research further points out that the systematic transformation of mainstream media requires the establishment of a collaborative system of \"technology - system - talent\", dynamically balancing ideological security and technological evolution in the process of upholding tradition and innovation, and ultimately promoting the high-quality and sustainable development of the radio and television industry driven by new quality productive forces.",
