  },
  "abstract_cn": "中国进入以高质量发展为导向的经济新常态，资本市场收并购日益频繁，控制权之争成为中国上市公司价值创造和资源配置效率的重要影响因素。本文以中国A股收并购中的控制权之争为考察对象，使用实证和案例分析相结合的方法，对其起因与动因、发生机制、经济后果等内容进行分析探讨。\n本文首先梳理了代理理论、控制权市场理论、公司治理理论等理论基础，构建了分析控制权争夺的理论框架。基于2010-2025年中国A股市场800个案例的实证分析发现：无实际控制人状态是控制权争夺的高危因素；协议收购成功率显著高于恶意收购；产业资本主导的收购成功率高于财务资本等。\n本文同时结合乾照光电控制权争夺案例分析，得出两次控制权争夺的成败原因。案例对比分析发现管理层的态度、收购的策略、产业的逻辑是决定控制权争夺成败的关键所在。\n研究得出九项重要实践启示：原大股东支持起决定性作用；充分尽调决定控制权取得战略；原董事会支持能加快交易进程；弹性交易方案能顺利实施变更；关键表决权的股权是取得控制权基础；取得董事会多数席位是控制权争夺关键抓手；管理团队支持助整合实施；产业协同稳固控制权；交易合规是必要条件。\n本研究即丰富了控制权转移的理论内涵，也为企业并购实践提供了有价值的参考，对控制权市场发展和演进具有重要意义。",
  "abstract_en": "China’s economy has stepped into a new normal focused on high-quality growth. Against this kind of backdrop, mergers and acquisitions (M&As) activity in the capital market has grown more frequent, and contests over corporate control have become a critical factor that impacts both value creation and resource allocation efficiency among Chinese listed firms. This paper centers on control contests in M&As involving China’s A-share listed companies, using a mix of empirical analysis and case studies to explore the causes, motivations, operational mechanisms, and economic consequences of these contests.\nThis study begins by reviewing agency theory, market for corporate control theory, and corporate governance theory and presents an analytical framework to examine control contests. Empirical studies among the 800 cases in Chinese A-share market during 2010-2025 suggest: nonexistence of actual controllers is a substantial risk to control contests, negotiated acquisition can make the control contest with 17% success rate superior to hostile acquisition with only 2.6% success rate, and the industrial capital is superior to financial capital to lead the acquisition with 30%.\nAlongside this empirical work, the paper also looks into a specific case—the control contest at Changelight-to unpack the reasons why two rounds of control contests there ended in success or failure. Comparing different aspects of this case shows that the management team’s stance, acquisition tactics, and industrial rationale are the critical factors that shape how a control contest turns out.\nThis research puts forward nine key practical takeaways: support from the original major shareholder carries decisive weight; comprehensive due diligence lays the groundwork for the strategy to secure control; backing from the original board of directors speeds up the transaction process; flexible transaction schemes make it easier to carry out control changes smoothly; equity holding key voting rights serves as the basis for securing control; securing a majority of board seats is a key way to prevail in control contests; backing from the management team helps push forward post-acquisition integration; industrial synergy helps solidify the control that’s been gained; and adhering to transaction rules is a must.\nThis study does more than just expand the theoretical meaning of control transfer, it also offers useful references for corporate M&A practices, and holds real significance for how the market for corporate control develops and evolves.",
